    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** (67.55) emerges as our primary play, buoyed by an ideal matchup against Sugano (4.80 xERA) and the premium value of his spot in the three-hole. Following closely, **Taylor Ward** (61.99) and **Daulton Varsho** (61.76) offer elite efficiency; **Taylor Ward** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor (+16%), while **Daulton Varsho** maintains a high floor due to his consistent order placement. Conversely, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (58.58) faces a daunting task against a tough lefty in S\u00e1nchez (2.86 xERA), suppressing what would otherwise be a top-tier score. We are keeping a close eye on **Bryson Stott** (59.45), whose value is constrained by the risk of facing a pitcher like Williams who historically holds runners well, potentially negating his sprint-speed utility in our pursuit of scarce SBs.\n\nThe most difficult decision was the final outfield slot, where **Tyler Freeman** (52.10) narrowly edged out **Gavin Sheets** (50.61). **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a neutral platoon and a stronger lineup spot (4th) compared to the platoon-taxed **Gavin Sheets**, who is forced into a challenging matchup against the lefty Springs. Further down the bench, we remain shorthanded at the catcher position with both **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** still relegated to the IL, while **Will Smith** remains out of the lineup entirely. We continue to monitor the utility bench\u2014including **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Jeremiah Jackson**\u2014but none provided the necessary statistical projection to displace our current starters. We must remain vigilant regarding **Jonathan Aranda**, whose 51.77 score is heavily threatened by a difficult assignment against Cole; any negative early-game indicators could warrant a quick pivot to conserve our valuable daily game caps.",
